docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:211:GOAL: <FOLDER_PATH> has 0 un-dispositioned PDFs. Every PDF ends either represented by a wiki/sources/*.md page (real ingest), folded into an existing page as a same-DOI rollup (with the wishlist row marked ingested), or marked in data/evidence/wishlist-fetch-audit.csv with an explicit skip:<reason> or fail:<reason> decision. Stop when met OR hard blocker (paper-internal contradiction, DOI conflict).
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:213:How: TRIAGE FIRST. Open every PDF in the folder in parallel batches of 10. Classify each as (a) real-ingest, (b) dedup-rollup, (c) skip:<reason>, (d) blocker. Batch-commit all (b)+(c) decisions to wishlist-fetch-audit.csv in one or two commits. Then real-ingest the (a) pile, batch-committing every ~10 source pages. Per CLAUDE.md Part 4, do NOT commit per-paper.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:215:Audit each new source page per audit-prompt.md (best-effort: commit with status=pending-audit-spawn-failed if spawn errors, do not stop). Routing audit (`npm run evidence:source-routes`) runs ONCE at session end. Frontmatter discipline per CLAUDE.md Part 5 — products/ingredients/matrices/metals/jurisdictions at the level of specificity the source states.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:219:Output: data/evidence/codex-runs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<HHMM>.md with goal-met state (folder count before/after), breakdown by disposition, commit hashes (with batch ranges).
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:231:Output: data/evidence/codex-runs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<HHMM>.md with pages filled, sections written per page, commit hashes.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:243:Output: data/evidence/codex-runs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<HHMM>.md with counter-before/counter-after, per-category fix counts, commit hashes.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:255:Output: data/evidence/codex-runs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<HHMM>.md with drafts written, commit hashes.
docs/codex-collaboration/README.md:286:In practice, the role split (audit vs ingest) makes this rare. Document any observed conflicts in `data/evidence/codex-runs/conflicts-<date>.md` so the role split can be tightened.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:12:GOAL: drain raw/manual-fetch/seasonal-geographic-variance/auto-fetched/ to 0 PDFs. The wishlist fetcher in the daemon is producing 100–250 PDFs/hour into this folder. You are the primary consumer alongside the Claude/Opus daemon, which picks up residuals at a hard per-tick cap of 3 PDFs as of 2026-05-28 (see tools/autonomy/ingest-manual-fetch-batch.mjs). Stop only when the folder is empty OR a named hard blocker fires (see ESCALATION below). No time budget. No "feels enough." No self-invented stop criteria. The earlier "drain to ≤10" threshold (pre-2026-05-28) left residuals stuck indefinitely: Codex would no-op on every fire whenever the queue dropped below 10, while the daemon also skipped this folder. Both ends now drain to zero.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:15:  ls raw/manual-fetch/seasonal-geographic-variance/auto-fetched/*.pdf > /tmp/codex-snapshot-$(date +%s).txt
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:19:STEP 2 — RACE-SAFE CLAIM. Before processing any PDF, check data/evidence/autonomy/manual-fetch-tracker.csv. If a row matches the PDF's filename AND status starts with "claimed" or "ingested", SKIP it (daemon may be mid-process). Otherwise add a row with status="claimed-by-codex" + a timestamp before touching the PDF. This prevents double-ingest races.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:24:  (c) skip:<reason> — false positive. Use existing vocabulary in data/evidence/wishlist-fetch-audit.csv (skip:no-heavy-metal-data / skip:not-target-cell / skip:not-food-occurrence / skip:review-only-no-primary-data / skip:not-pdf:<content-type>)
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:27:Batch-commit ALL (b)+(c) decisions to data/evidence/wishlist-fetch-audit.csv in ONE commit titled:
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:28:  triage sweep <date> <time>: <K> rollups + <P> skips
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:48:  ingest auto-fetched <date> <time> batch N: K source pages
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:53:STEP 5 — UPDATE TRACKER. After each source page is committed, update its row in data/evidence/autonomy/manual-fetch-tracker.csv to status="ingested-by-codex" with the commit hash.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:55:STEP 6 — AUDIT (best-effort). After each batch, try to spawn fresh-context audits per docs/gpt-collaboration/audit-prompt.md (5 checks: numerical fidelity, slug vocabulary, speciation/methods, brand firewall, wiki/HMTc firewall). If `agent thread limit reached`, write each page's audit-queue row with status=pending-audit-spawn-failed and CONTINUE. NEVER stop on spawn failure — Claude drains the async-audit lane separately.
docs/codex-collaboration/sprint-ingest-prompt.md:58:  node tools/autonomy/auto-fetched-hygiene.mjs --report
